From: p5r-proton
Subject: ntdll: restore Wine 7 yield, delay and signal-and-wait semantics

Persona 5 Royal is CPU bound on modern Proton even though the GPU is mostly
idle, and the regression is already present between GE-Proton 7 and 8.  The
modern paths add measurable overhead to synchronization primitives that the
game uses on hot paths:

- NtYieldExecution() no longer performs two getrusage(RUSAGE_THREAD) calls
  and always reports STATUS_SUCCESS on a successful sched_yield(), as in
  Wine 7.  Sleep(0)/SwitchToThread() pay one syscall instead of three.
- NtDelayExecution() uses usleep(0) for the implicit yield again and no
  longer returns STATUS_NO_YIELD_PERFORMED for zero timeouts.  The alertable
  path goes straight to the server, matching Wine 7.
- NtSignalAndWaitForSingleObject() performs the signal and wait atomically
  in the server again.  The in-process/fsync path needs two separate
  operations and measures roughly twice as slow for this API.

The rest of the modern synchronization code is left untouched.
